WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.660
Jason pointed to the screen.

2
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.961
"We're making bread today!"

3
00:00:20.021 --> 00:00:21.262
Nina yawned loudly.

4
00:00:21.282 --> 00:00:23.862
"Excuse me."

5
00:00:25.243 --> 00:00:26.063
Chef frowned.

6
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:29.264
"Nina, are you bored with cooking?"

7
00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:32.417
Nina felt embarrassed.

8
00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:34.879
"Oh, no, Chef!

9
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.061
My little sister has an earache.

10
00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:41.123
She woke up last night crying.

11
00:00:41.143 --> 00:00:43.565
I didn't sleep well."

12
00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:45.447
"I see.

13
00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:48.549
Well, try to stay awake today in class."

14
00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:50.170
Nina nodded.

15
00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.013
Chef put four large bowls on the counter.

16
00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.256
He gave everyone a plastic bag.

17
00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:01.353
"Mix your dough in these bags.

18
00:01:02.514 --> 00:01:05.596
Putting the bags in a bowl makes it easier to add ingredients."

19
00:01:05.616 --> 00:01:08.878
"Poor Lulu!"

20
00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:10.139
Izzie whispered.

21
00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:12.621
"Earaches hurt!"

22
00:01:14.222 --> 00:01:14.962
Nina nodded.

23
00:01:14.982 --> 00:01:18.605
"Mom is bringing her to the doctor today."

24
00:01:20.106 --> 00:01:21.887
The kids put their bags in the bowls.

25
00:01:23.108 --> 00:01:26.210
They poured in one cup of flour and three tablespoons of sugar.

26
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.212
Then they added the yeast and warm water.

27
00:01:30.888 --> 00:01:32.029
"Now seal your bags.

28
00:01:33.029 --> 00:01:35.571
Make sure all the air is out," Chef said.

29
00:01:37.332 --> 00:01:39.733
The kids sealed the bags and mixed the ingredients.

30
00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.835
Bobby read from the recipe.

31
00:01:44.275 --> 00:01:46.857
"Let dough sit for ten to fifteen minutes."

32
00:01:48.638 --> 00:01:49.698
His face lit up.

33
00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:52.080
"Let's go outside!"

34
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.062
"No, we'll learn something instead," Chef said.

35
00:02:00.848 --> 00:02:02.209
"Yeast is a fungus.

36
00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.031
The warm water activates it.

37
00:02:06.572 --> 00:02:09.654
The yeast feeds off the sugar, and it starts fermenting.

38
00:02:12.756 --> 00:02:14.457
That makes the dough rise."

39
00:02:16.218 --> 00:02:19.240
Izzie made a face.

40
00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.562
"Ew! We're eating fungus!"

41
00:02:21.582 --> 00:02:24.384
"Do you eat mushrooms?

42
00:02:25.264 --> 00:02:27.146
They're a fungus," Jason said.

43
00:02:27.166 --> 00:02:31.472
"That's right," Chef said.

44
00:02:33.433 --> 00:02:35.494
Soon it was time to add more ingredients.

45
00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:40.737
The kids added salt, olive oil, and another cup of flour.

46
00:02:44.758 --> 00:02:45.859
mix everything together.

47
00:02:47.139 --> 00:02:50.041
Then we add the last cup of flour," Jason said.

48
00:02:52.022 --> 00:02:52.962
Bobby sighed.

49
00:02:52.982 --> 00:02:56.624
"And mix again."

50
00:02:58.728 --> 00:03:01.610
Chef laid out parchment paper and sprinkled it with flour.

51
00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.731
"Put flour on your hands too.

52
00:03:05.612 --> 00:03:07.313
That way the dough won't stick to them."

53
00:03:08.974 --> 00:03:10.815
The kids placed their dough on the paper.

54
00:03:12.456 --> 00:03:14.257
Chef set the timer for ten minutes.

55
00:03:14.277 --> 00:03:17.239
"We knead for ten minutes.

56
00:03:18.439 --> 00:03:21.041
Kneading dough makes me feel better when I'm in a bad mood."

57
00:03:21.061 --> 00:03:26.664
"I hope it works today," Bobby whispered to Jason.

58
00:03:27.764 --> 00:03:28.685
Jason laughed.

59
00:03:33.908 --> 00:03:35.950
Suddenly Nina had an idea.

60
00:03:39.092 --> 00:03:40.213
She pounded her dough.

61
00:03:41.774 --> 00:03:42.554
She folded it.

62
00:03:44.376 --> 00:03:45.156
She squeezed it.

63
00:03:45.176 --> 00:03:48.258
"Take that, you mean earache!"

64
00:03:48.779 --> 00:03:49.319
she thought.

65
00:03:49.339 --> 00:03:52.541
"Stop hurting Lulu!"

66
00:03:54.122 --> 00:03:56.484
The other kids got tired, but Nina didn't.

67
00:03:57.616 --> 00:03:58.477
She kept kneading.

68
00:03:59.958 --> 00:04:02.900
When the timer went off, they formed loaves with the dough.

69
00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.302
They covered the loaves with warm, damp towels.

70
00:04:06.322 --> 00:04:09.084
"The dough needs to rise.

71
00:04:10.145 --> 00:04:11.946
Time to clean up," Chef said.

72
00:04:13.487 --> 00:04:16.729
The kids washed dishes, wiped the counters, and swept the floor.

73
00:04:16.749 --> 00:04:22.253
"I'm going to give my loaf to Lulu," Nina said to Izzie.

74
00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:24.174
Izzie grinned.

75
00:04:24.194 --> 00:04:26.176
"Good idea."

76
00:04:27.888 --> 00:04:30.969
"Cool!" Bobby pointed to the loaves.

77
00:04:30.989 --> 00:04:32.569
"They're rising!"

78
00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.090
Chef nodded.

79
00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:40.572
"The yeast gives off carbon dioxide and makes the bread rise."

80
00:04:43.352 --> 00:04:44.933
Soon he put the loaves in the oven.

81
00:04:47.533 --> 00:04:50.254
A while later Nina's mother walked in with Lulu.

82
00:04:55.376 --> 00:04:56.616
let's go outside.

83
00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.201
I'll show you the animals!"

84
00:04:59.561 --> 00:05:00.242
Nina said.

85
00:05:02.363 --> 00:05:04.085
Lulu met the goats and chickens.

86
00:05:05.746 --> 00:05:07.087
She loved petting Cinnamon.

87
00:05:10.189 --> 00:05:12.611
When the bread was ready, they went back inside.

88
00:05:17.354 --> 00:05:19.916
Lulu! I made this bread for you!"

89
00:05:20.276 --> 00:05:20.976
Nina said.

90
00:05:22.037 --> 00:05:22.998
Lulu clapped.

91
00:05:24.039 --> 00:05:25.840
"Lulu is all better!"
